@PACKAGE@ in Sparky Stereo OS
@UNDERLINE@

This is NVIDIA's package @PACKAGE@ @NV_VERSION@ from NVIDIA's CUDA
repository for Debian 12, carried by Sparky Stereo OS at version
@VERSION@,
for the Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards that the edition's open kernel
modules (Turing and newer) do not run. NVIDIA's 580 branch is the last
for these cards, and NVIDIA publishes it for Debian only in that repository,
whose key Debian 14's APT refuses (its binding signature is SHA-1).
When the edition builds this package, gpgv checks NVIDIA's signature on the
repository's Release file with NVIDIA's key, the Release file gives the
index's SHA-256, and the index gives this package's; the edition's key signs
the edition's repository.

What is NVIDIA's
----------------

Every file of the package is NVIDIA's, byte for byte as NVIDIA ships it, with
its mode, and so are its maintainer scripts. The NVIDIA Software License
distributes the binary files only unmodified (sections 1.1(d)(i) and 2.3) and
asks that a modified file carry a prominent notice of the change (section
2.5), so no file of NVIDIA's is changed. Lean Code, which removes comments
from the edition's text files, leaves each of them as NVIDIA ships it:
"dpkg-stereo --status" and the manifest named below give that reason for
each. NVIDIA's licence is in this folder's copyright file, NVIDIA's text byte
for byte. NVIDIA ships its i386 packages and its cuda-drivers meta packages
without that file; the edition adds it to them, the same file NVIDIA's amd64
packages ship, so that the licence goes to each recipient of the software
(section 1.1(d)(ii)) and every package has its copyright file (Debian Policy
2.3).

What is the edition's
---------------------

- The control file: the version, NVIDIA's exact relations among the carried
  packages at that version; the kernel dependency stays at the published
  nvidia-legacy-580xx-kernel-dkms provider's version. Also the maintainer (NVIDIA
  stays as Original-Maintainer), the homepage, the bug tracker and a note in
  the description; and, where NVIDIA's package ships programs or libraries
  but declares no dependency at all (libnvidia-nscq), the dependency
  dpkg-shlibdeps derives from them; and, in nvidia-kernel-support, no Provides, Conflicts or Replaces of nvidia-detect (Debian's
  nvidia-detect is the real detector Hardware Setup runs and shares no file with it). This file is the notice of that change.
- Three files: this one; changelog.Debian.ARCHITECTURE.gz in this folder,
  the edition's changelog entry (NVIDIA's own changelog stays as it is); and
  the Lean Code manifest /usr/share/dpkg-stereo/lc/@PACKAGE@/ARCHITECTURE.json,
  which lists every file with its SHA-256.

Packaging: Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's (Capitain Jack) edition of
SparkyLinux (https://sparkylinux.org, by Paweł "pavroo" Pijanowski).
Problems with this package go to the edition's tracker,
https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues, not to NVIDIA.

Source of the carry
-------------------

The edition source package is nvidia-graphics-drivers at @VERSION@.
It contains this carry recipe, the vendor file manifest with hashes and HTTPS
origins, the verification key and the licence. It retains the exact licensed vendor package inputs for offline rebuilding,
without claiming to contain the proprietary driver source. The build verifies
each retained archive and refuses a checksum mismatch.
The existing driver lock selects this source name; the unchanged DKMS provider
remains at 580.196.07-1+sparky2+lc1.
